<item><title>Kenya uses KSh4.6 billion to hold diesel price at KSh227.76</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenya-uses-ksh4-6-billion-to-hold-diesel-price-at-ksh227-76-23c980/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenya-uses-ksh4-6-billion-to-hold-diesel-price-at-ksh227-76-23c980/</guid><category>Kenya</category><description>The fuel regulator kept Nairobi’s diesel ceiling unchanged through 14 December after import costs rose 6.7% in October.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:39:10 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenya-uses-ksh4-6-billion-to-hold-diesel-price-at-ksh227-76-23c980/share.jpg" length="40907" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenya-uses-ksh4-6-billion-to-hold-diesel-price-at-ksh227-76-23c980/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
